      "incumbent": true,
      "summary": "Brian Babin is the incumbent U.S. Representative for Texas's 36th Congressional District, first elected in 2014. He serves as Chairman of the House Committee on Science, Space, and Technology and previously chaired the Space Subcommittee. A dentist by profession and U.S. Air Force veteran, Babin focuses on border security, tax cuts, Second Amendment rights, and space exploration. He has held the seat since 2015 and won the 2026 Republican primary with 81.1% of the vote against challenger Jonathan Mitchell.",
