      "party": "Democratic",
      "incumbent": false,
      "summary": "Rhonda Hart is the Democratic nominee for Texas's 36th Congressional District. An Army veteran who served from 2000 to 2003, her daughter Kimberly Vaughan was killed in the 2018 Santa Fe High School shooting, leading Hart to become a prominent gun-safety activist. She previously ran for Congress in Texas's 14th Congressional District in 2024. Hart advocates for common-sense gun laws, women's reproductive rights, and improved veterans' healthcare. She won the 2026 Democratic primary with 64.1% of the vote, defeating Doug Rogers.",
